      "role": "user",
      "content": "right but regulations only work if people actually monitor what's happening behind closed doors. these companies have way more money and tech than the regulators do. if they were using the foot sensors to map out personality traits or emotional stability to sell to advertisers or something, they'd just bury it in the fine print or hide it in the cloud processing. dont you think it's more likely that the \"technical capability\" is actually being used under the radar, rather than just being a \"theoretical\" thing?",
